The Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) announced the final Medicare Part B premium on November 17, 2026, in a CMS fact sheet. The standard monthly premium is $209.40, which is up $6.50 from $202.90.

In our internal calculation, a retiree with a $2,000 monthly benefit receives a raise of $72.00. Subtracting the $6.50 Medicare increase leaves $65.50 a month before other deductions.